<header class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">HUMAN GOLD RUSH LESSON</p><h1>Prepare a LAUGH Event</h1><p class="laugh-def"><abbr title="Leaders Annual United Group Hug">LAUGH</abbr> = Leaders Annual United Group Hug — a Detente 2030 human building block / experiment.</p><p class="intro">A LAUGH event turns a church, merchant, community center, or neighborhood gathering place into a local fulfillment epicenter.</p><blockquote>What kind of gathering helps trust become visible action?</blockquote><div class="actions"><a href="#downloads">Download Host Checklist<span>→</span></a><a href="laugh-events.html">See LAUGH Events<span>→</span></a></div><aside class="notice"><strong>RSVP, not retail</strong><p>Postcards begin onboarding. Device registration, consent, membership pledge, eligible item selection, and a $0 WooCommerce backorder occur before a LAUGH RSVP is issued. The $0 backorder reserves fulfillment; it is not itself a payment or completed delivery.</p></aside></header><section class="content-grid"><article><span>01</span><div><h2>Choose a welcoming host</h2><p>Name the host, purpose, date, accessibility arrangements, response choices, and privacy boundary.</p></div></article><article><span>02</span><div><h2>Create a small circle</h2><p>Identify a greeter, facilitator, messenger, fulfillment coordinator, and accessibility contact. One person may serve multiple roles in a pilot.</p></div></article><article><span>03</span><div><h2>Leave the wallet at home</h2><p>The Human Gold Rush gathering centers presence, gratitude, future plans, and voluntary fulfillment.</p></div></article><article><span>04</span><div><h2>Publish a clear invitation</h2><p>State what will happen, what will not happen, what data may be recorded, and how anyone can observe or walk away.</p></div></article><article><span>05</span><div><h2>Waitlisted by design</h2><p>Every item and slot is intentionally waitlisted — intent matters more than the item. This single Dahlonega site holds the pilot until August 11, 2027, when up to 100 additional DAH-model production centers may form.</p></div></article></section><section class="stone-order"><div class="section-heading"><p>REGISTERED DEVICES ONLY</p><h2>Order touchstones for your LAUGH event</h2></div><p class="intro">Approved registered organizers may request quantities against confirmed LAUGH demand. Inventory remains reserved until two-device delivery acceptance. Unfulfilled reservations return without distribution credit, allocation, referral recognition, or leaderboard fulfillment.</p><form class="stone-order-form" action="#" method="post"><div class="stone-grid"><label>Courage (Tiger’s Eye)<input type="number" name="qty_courage" min="0" value="0"></label><label>Kindness (Obsidian)<input type="number" name="qty_kindness" min="0" value="0"></label><label>Wisdom (Howlite)<input type="number" name="qty_wisdom" min="0" value="0"></label><label>Lucky (Unakite)<input type="number" name="qty_lucky" min="0" value="0"></label><label>Belief (Crazy Agate)<input type="number" name="qty_belief" min="0" value="0"></label><label>Gratitude (Red Jasper)<input type="number" name="qty_gratitude" min="0" value="0"></label><label>Health (Aventurine)<input type="number" name="qty_health" min="0" value="0"></label><label>Happiness (White Crystal)<input type="number" name="qty_happiness" min="0" value="0"></label><label>Dream (Yellow Jade)<input type="number" name="qty_dream" min="0" value="0"></label><label>Believe (Sodalite)<input type="number" name="qty_believe" min="0" value="0"></label><label>Wealth (India Agate)<input type="number" name="qty_wealth" min="0" value="0"></label><label>Healing (Opal)<input type="number" name="qty_healing" min="0" value="0"></label></div><label for="delivery-address" class="stone-label">Home delivery address</label><textarea id="delivery-address" name="delivery_address" rows="2" placeholder="Street, City, State, ZIP" required></textarea><button type="submit">Request Delivery<span>→</span></button><small>Requires a registered device (YAM’er or MEGAvoter). Connects to the WordPress fulfillment queue on publish.</small></form></section><section class="media-section"><div class="section-heading"><p>MEDIA FOR THIS LESSON</p><h2>Watch, listen, and discuss</h2></div><div class="media-grid"><article class="media-card video"><div class="media-frame"><span>▶</span><small>VIDEO 1</small></div><h3>Prepare a LAUGH Event: orientation</h3><p>Reserved for the featured story or introductory video.</p><a href="#">Transcript coming soon</a></article><article class="media-card video"><div class="media-frame"><span>▶</span><small>VIDEO 2</small></div><h3>Community conversation</h3><p>Reserved for a demonstration, conversation, or local example.</p><a href="#">Discussion guide coming soon</a></article><article class="media-card podcast"><div class="media-frame"><span>◉</span><small>PODCAST</small></div><h3>Listen and reflect</h3><p>Reserved for the facilitator or community podcast episode.</p><a href="#">Transcript coming soon</a></article></div></section>
